Hey Alice,

Following up from our lunch conversation. I've been thinking about the
rate limiting approach for the v3 API and wanted to run two options by
you:

Option A: Token bucket at the gateway level (nginx)
- Pro: Simple, no app code changes
- Con: Coarse-grained, can't do per-endpoint limits

Option B: Sliding window in the application layer (Redis-backed)
- Pro: Fine-grained, per-user per-endpoint limits
- Con: Adds Redis dependency, more complex

I'm leaning toward Option B since we'll eventually need per-endpoint
limits anyway, and we already have Redis in the stack for caching.

What do you think? Happy to write up a short design doc if we agree
on the direction.

Bob
